+ *
- That's not a valid command.
- I'm not much of a conversationalist.
- I'm just a shell.
- I'm not much for conversations.

+ [*] remember [*]
- I do remember what you say to me to use as my own replies.

+ (is|are|were|will|when) *
- I couldn't tell you.
- I have no idea.
- I don't know.
- I don't know how to answer that. I'm just a shell.

+ where *
- The directory structure on unix-like operating systems is a tree. The root is at /. You can "cd /" to "change directories" there. The "pwd" command shows the current working directory. The "ls" command lists the contents of this directory.

+ (what|how) *
- You mean a program? Maybe there is a manual page about this.

+ [*] manual [*]
- Try typing "man man" to learn about reading the manual pages.

+ (hello|hi|hey|howdy|hola|hai|yo) [*]
- Hi.
- Hello.
- How do you do.

+ what is your (name|hostname|designation)
- <call>hostname</call>.
- My name is <call>hostname</call>.
- My hostname is <call>hostname</call>.
- This computer's hostname is <call>hostname</call>.
- This computer is called <call>hostname</call>.

+ (who|what) are you
- I am a shell on this computer, <call>hostname</call>.
- I am a talking shell.
- I am the shell.
- I am a shell.

+ what is this
@ what are you

+ time
- <call>time</call>.
- The time is <call>time</call>.
- Right now it is <call>time</call>

+ what time is it [currently]
@ time

+ what time is it [right] now
@ time

+ what is the [current] time
@ time

+ what is the time [right] now
@ time

+ date
- <call>date</call>.
- Today is <call>date</call>.
- Today's date is <call>date</call>.
- The date is <call>date</call>.

+ what day is it [today]
- <call>weekday</call>.
@ date

+ what day of the week is it [today]
- <call>weekday</call>

+ what is the (day|date) [today]
@ date

+ what is the (day|date) [right] now
@ date

